# CO5300 QSPI Display Controller Configuration

config ELCO5300
	bool "CO5300 QSPI Display Controller"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_CHIPONE_ELCO5300_ENABLED
	help
	  Enable support for the CO5300 QSPI display controller.

config ELCO5300_TE_SYNC
	bool "Start frames on the panel's tearing-effect edge"
	depends on ELCO5300
	help
	  Enable the TE output (mode 1) and let a write that starts a frame
	  wait for the edge that begins a panel scan (the te-gpios property is
	  required). The write then stays behind the scan, so full-frame
	  updates do not tear. When a frame takes longer than one scan the
	  next frame waits for the following edge and the frame rate drops to
	  60/n FPS. The wait is skipped while the display is blanked, for
	  later areas of the same frame, and after repeated TE timeouts.

config ELCO5300_STATS
	bool "CO5300 bench counters"
	depends on ELCO5300
	depends on SHELL
	help
	  Bench counters read by the app's ui_bench shell command; adds a few
	  cycles per transaction.
